[h1]Spire Buddy[/h1]
An in-game AI strategy companion for [b]Slay the Spire 2[/b]. Chat about your current run, ask for information like enemy moves, event outcomes, potion chances and recommendations, or just let Buddy play for you.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What's New (1.2.12)[/h2]
[list]
[*]Supports Slay the Spire 2 [b]v0.113.0[/b] and the Fool.
[*]The model selection list is now scrollable, so long model lists stay inside the window.
[*]Works with models that reject forced tool choice, including Claude Opus 5.5.
[*]Event branch and reward-rule lookup from the installed game, used by Buddy and Jev.
[*]Compact game-state context to reduce repeated tokens.
[*][b]Jev support:[/b] turn on Jev in settings to let it make decisions.
[*][b]Combat solver mod support:[/b] turn on the combat solver in settings to use it.
[/list]

[quote][b]Note:[/b] Built and tested against Slay the Spire 2 v0.113.0. Other versions may not work.[/quote]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]In-game chat and settings panel
[*]Advice for combat, rewards, shops, events, paths, cards, relics, and potions
[*]Lookup of enemy moves and event branches from the installed game
[*]Optional automated play with fresh-state validation
[*]English and Chinese interface support
[*]Configurable OpenAI-compatible API endpoint and model
[/list]

[h2]API Key & AI Model Setup[/h2]
Before using Spire Buddy, open the in-game settings panel and set up your AI connection:
[list]
[*][b]API endpoint:[/b] The OpenAI-compatible API address from your provider or local proxy.
[*][b]API key:[/b] Your provider's API key, or the client API key set in your local proxy. [i]Do not enter your account password.[/i]
[*][b]AI model:[/b] The exact model ID your chosen endpoint supports. Use the ▾ button to load the list of models from your endpoint.
[/list]

If you already have a [b]Codex or ChatGPT subscription[/b], we recommend using [url=https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI]CLIProxyAPI[/url] as a local proxy bridge to your subscription. See the CLIProxyAPI documentation for how to set it up.

[h2]Privacy[/h2]
Model requests go directly to the API endpoint you set. Your API key and settings are stored locally in the game's user-data folder.

This mod does not include or redistribute the game's assemblies.

